IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`
IMPORT `oas-core-measures`
IMPORT `oa3-helpers`

-- Old Age Security Regulations (C.R.C., c. 1246), Part I (Applications): regulations 24 to 28.1: who may be paid for a
-- beneficiary (24), the notices an applicant or beneficiary must give (25), suspension (26), cancelling a pension or supplement
-- (26.1), recovering an overpayment (27) and deductions from a benefit for provincial or municipal advances (28.1).
--
-- "Forthwith" (reg 25(1) and (2)) and "immediately" (reg 25(3) and (4)) are not measured by the text, so the encoding does not
-- pick a number of days for them: it computes the day on which the duty arises, and takes "the notice was given forthwith"
-- as a fact the person states (fork F-25 in NOTES.md). Where the text does measure a time (one month of his return, six
-- months after payment begins) the deadline is computed with the keel's `the day that is _ after _`.

§ `PART I Applications`

§§ `Payment to Person other than Beneficiary`

-- 24(1): the Minister may direct a benefit to be paid for a beneficiary who is incapable of managing his own affairs. To whom:
-- (a) a person or agency the Minister is satisfied is authorized by a law of Canada or of a province to manage his affairs;
-- or (b), where the Minister is not satisfied that any is so authorized, a person or agency the Minister appoints that has
-- entered into an agreement with the Minister. (a) is looked at first: (b) is only "where" (a) fails.
DECLARE `reg 24(1): Whom the Minister may direct the benefit to be paid to on behalf of the beneficiary` IS ONE OF
    `reg 24(1)(a): a person or agency authorized by or pursuant to a law of Canada or of a province to manage the affairs of the beneficiary`
    `reg 24(1)(b): a person or agency the Minister appoints that has entered into an agreement with the Minister to administer and expend the benefit`
    `reg 24(1): No person or agency under this subsection`

-- src:261 | 24 (1) Where a person or agency provides evidence satisfactory to the Minister that a beneficiary, by reason of infirmity, illness, insanity or other cause, is incapable of managing his own affairs, the Minister may direct the benefit to be paid on behalf of such beneficiary
-- src:262 | (a) to any person or agency that the Minister is satisfied is authorized by or pursuant to any law of Canada or of a province to manage the affairs of that beneficiary; or
-- src:263 | (b) where the Minister is not satisfied that any person or agency is so authorized, to any person or agency that the Minister may appoint for such purpose and that has entered into an agreement with the Minister to administer and expend the benefit on behalf of that beneficiary in accordance with the terms of the agreement.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 24(1) (src:261-263)
GIVEN `evidence satisfactory to the Minister has been provided by a person or agency that the beneficiary is incapable of managing his own affairs by reason of infirmity, illness, insanity or other cause` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that a person or agency is authorized by or pursuant to a law of Canada or of a province to manage the affairs of the beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a person or agency that the Minister may appoint has entered into an agreement with the Minister to administer and expend the benefit on behalf of the beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `reg 24(1): Whom the Minister may direct the benefit to be paid to on behalf of the beneficiary`
`reg 24(1): the person or agency to whom the Minister may direct the benefit to be paid on behalf of the beneficiary` `evidence satisfactory to the Minister has been provided by a person or agency that the beneficiary is incapable of managing his own affairs by reason of infirmity, illness, insanity or other cause` `the Minister is satisfied that a person or agency is authorized by or pursuant to a law of Canada or of a province to manage the affairs of the beneficiary` `a person or agency that the Minister may appoint has entered into an agreement with the Minister to administer and expend the benefit on behalf of the beneficiary` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `evidence satisfactory to the Minister has been provided by a person or agency that the beneficiary is incapable of managing his own affairs by reason of infirmity, illness, insanity or other cause`
            THEN `reg 24(1): No person or agency under this subsection`
        IF `the Minister is satisfied that a person or agency is authorized by or pursuant to a law of Canada or of a province to manage the affairs of the beneficiary`
            THEN `reg 24(1)(a): a person or agency authorized by or pursuant to a law of Canada or of a province to manage the affairs of the beneficiary`
        IF `a person or agency that the Minister may appoint has entered into an agreement with the Minister to administer and expend the benefit on behalf of the beneficiary`
            THEN `reg 24(1)(b): a person or agency the Minister appoints that has entered into an agreement with the Minister to administer and expend the benefit`
        OTHERWISE `reg 24(1): No person or agency under this subsection`

-- 24(2): the Minister shall furnish directions to a person or agency appointed under (1) to receive a benefit.
-- src:264 | (2) The Minister shall furnish to a person or agency appointed under subsection (1) to receive a benefit such directions regarding the administration and expenditure of the benefit as the Minister considers in the best interests of the beneficiary.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 24(2) (src:264)
GIVEN `a person or agency has been appointed under subsection (1) to receive a benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 24(2): the Minister must furnish directions regarding the administration and expenditure of the benefit in the best interests of the beneficiary` `a person or agency has been appointed under subsection (1) to receive a benefit` MEANS
    `a person or agency has been appointed under subsection (1) to receive a benefit`

-- 24(3): a person or agency appointed shall account for the payments received and disbursements made, in the form and at the
-- times the Minister requires.
-- src:265 | (3) Any person or agency appointed under subsection (1) shall account for the benefit payments received and the disbursements made, the account to be in such form and to be made at such times as the Minister may require.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 24(3) (src:265)
GIVEN `a person or agency has been appointed under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person or agency has accounted for the benefit payments received and the disbursements made in the form and at the times the Minister requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 24(3): the person or agency has met the duty to account` `a person or agency has been appointed under subsection (1)` `the person or agency has accounted for the benefit payments received and the disbursements made in the form and at the times the Minister requires` MEANS
        (NOT `a person or agency has been appointed under subsection (1)`)
    OR  `the person or agency has accounted for the benefit payments received and the disbursements made in the form and at the times the Minister requires`

-- 24(4): where a benefit is paid to a person or agency to administer for the beneficiary, the notices required by section 25 are
-- given by that person or agency (and not by the beneficiary).
-- src:266 | (4) Where a benefit is paid to any person or agency to be administered and expended for and on behalf of a beneficiary, the notices required by section 25 shall be given by such person or agency.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 24(4) (src:266)
GIVEN `the benefit is paid to a person or agency to be administered and expended for and on behalf of the beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Party
`reg 24(4): the party who must give the notices required by regulation 25` `the benefit is paid to a person or agency to be administered and expended for and on behalf of the beneficiary` MEANS
    IF `the benefit is paid to a person or agency to be administered and expended for and on behalf of the beneficiary`
    THEN Representative
    ELSE Beneficiary

-- 24(5): a benefit payment may be made to the estate of a deceased beneficiary or, if there is no estate, to a person or agency the
-- Minister designates, where (a) an amount is payable as a benefit to the deceased, or (b) a payment made to the beneficiary or
-- on the beneficiary's behalf is returned to the Minister after the beneficiary's death.
-- src:267 | (5) A benefit payment may be made to the estate of a deceased beneficiary or, if there is no estate, to a person or agency designated by the Minister, where
-- src:268 | (a) an amount is payable as a benefit to the deceased beneficiary; or
-- src:269 | (b) a benefit payment made to the beneficiary or made on behalf of the beneficiary by cheque or otherwise is returned to the Minister after the beneficiary’s death.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 24(5) (src:267-269)
GIVEN `an amount is payable as a benefit to the deceased beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a benefit payment made to the beneficiary or on the beneficiary's behalf by cheque or otherwise is returned to the Minister after the beneficiary's death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is an estate of the deceased beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Party
`reg 24(5): the party to whom a benefit payment may be made after the beneficiary's death` `an amount is payable as a benefit to the deceased beneficiary` `a benefit payment made to the beneficiary or on the beneficiary's behalf by cheque or otherwise is returned to the Minister after the beneficiary's death` `there is an estate of the deceased beneficiary` MEANS
    IF `an amount is payable as a benefit to the deceased beneficiary` OR `a benefit payment made to the beneficiary or on the beneficiary's behalf by cheque or otherwise is returned to the Minister after the beneficiary's death`
    THEN JUST (IF `there is an estate of the deceased beneficiary` THEN Estate ELSE Representative)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Notices by or on Behalf of an Applicant or Beneficiary`

-- 25(1): an applicant or beneficiary absent from Canada for a period in excess of one month shall forthwith give notice of
-- it, and within one month of his return shall notify the Minister of his return. The absence is "in excess of one month" from
-- the first day after the day one month after he left; the notice of the absence is due "forthwith", which the text does not
-- measure (fork F-25 in NOTES.md), so the day the duty arises is what is computed. The notice of the return is due by the day
-- one month after. For a person still away the end of the absence is the day the question is asked.
-- src:272 | 25 (1) Where an applicant or a beneficiary has absented himself from Canada for a period in excess of one month, he shall forthwith give notice thereof to the Minister and within one month of his return to Canada shall notify the Minister of his return.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 25(1) (src:272)
GIVEN `the day on which the applicant or beneficiary left Canada` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the absence ended, or the day on which the question is asked if it has not ended` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 25(1): the applicant or beneficiary has absented himself from Canada for a period in excess of one month` `the day on which the applicant or beneficiary left Canada` `the day on which the absence ended, or the day on which the question is asked if it has not ended` MEANS
    `the day on which the absence ended, or the day on which the question is asked if it has not ended` GREATER THAN (`the day that is` (`a limit in months` 1) `after` `the day on which the applicant or beneficiary left Canada`)

@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 25(1) (src:272)
GIVEN `the day on which the applicant or beneficiary left Canada` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 25(1): the first day on which the absence is in excess of one month` `the day on which the applicant or beneficiary left Canada` MEANS
    (`the day that is` (`a limit in months` 1) `after` `the day on which the applicant or beneficiary left Canada`) PLUS 1

@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 25(1) (src:272)
GIVEN `the day on which the applicant or beneficiary returned to Canada` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 25(1): the last day on which the Minister may be notified of the return` `the day on which the applicant or beneficiary returned to Canada` MEANS
    `the day that is` (`a limit in months` 1) `after` `the day on which the applicant or beneficiary returned to Canada`

@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 25(1) (src:272)
GIVEN `the absence was in excess of one month` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice of the absence was given forthwith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the applicant or beneficiary returned to Canada` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the Minister was notified of the return` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 25(1): the applicant or beneficiary has given the notices` `the absence was in excess of one month` `notice of the absence was given forthwith` `the day on which the applicant or beneficiary returned to Canada` `the day on which the Minister was notified of the return` MEANS
        (NOT `the absence was in excess of one month`)
    OR  (    `notice of the absence was given forthwith`
         AND `the Minister was notified of the return in time`)
    WHERE
        `the Minister was notified of the return in time` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day on which the Minister was notified of the return`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST notified THEN notified AT MOST (`reg 25(1): the last day on which the Minister may be notified of the return` `the day on which the applicant or beneficiary returned to Canada`)

-- 25(2): the applicant or beneficiary shall notify the Minister of the address to which the benefit is to be sent and, forthwith,
-- of any change of it.
-- src:273 | (2) An applicant or a beneficiary shall notify the Minister of the address to which his benefit is to be sent and, in the event of any change of such address, shall forthwith notify the Minister of the change.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 25(2) (src:273)
GIVEN `the person is an applicant or a beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the address to which the benefit is to be sent has changed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 25(2): the person must forthwith notify the Minister of a change of the address to which the benefit is to be sent` `the person is an applicant or a beneficiary` `the address to which the benefit is to be sent has changed` MEANS
        `the person is an applicant or a beneficiary`
    AND `the address to which the benefit is to be sent has changed`

@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 25(2) (src:273)
GIVEN `the person is an applicant or a beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 25(2): the person must notify the Minister of the address to which the benefit is to be sent` `the person is an applicant or a beneficiary` MEANS
    `the person is an applicant or a beneficiary`

-- 25(3): joint applicants for an allowance who become separated: the beneficiary and the pensioner shall immediately notify.
-- src:274 | (3) Where joint applicants for an allowance become separated, the beneficiary and the pensioner shall immediately notify the Minister thereof.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 25(3) (src:274)
GIVEN `the joint applicants for an allowance have become separated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF Party
`reg 25(3): the parties who must immediately notify the Minister of the separation` `the joint applicants for an allowance have become separated` MEANS
    IF `the joint applicants for an allowance have become separated`
    THEN LIST Beneficiary, Pensioner
    ELSE EMPTY

-- 25(4): the beneficiary of an allowance dies: the pensioner shall immediately notify.
-- src:275 | (4) Where the beneficiary of an allowance dies, the pensioner shall immediately notify the Minister thereof.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 25(4) (src:275)
GIVEN `the beneficiary of an allowance has died` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF Party
`reg 25(4): the parties who must immediately notify the Minister of the death` `the beneficiary of an allowance has died` MEANS
    IF `the beneficiary of an allowance has died`
    THEN LIST Pensioner
    ELSE EMPTY

§§ `Suspension of Payments`

-- 26(1): the Minister shall suspend payment where it appears to the Minister that the beneficiary is ineligible, and may suspend
-- it where it appears that further inquiry into eligibility is necessary; the suspension continues until evidence satisfactory
-- to the Minister is given that the beneficiary is eligible. Both limbs turn on what "appears to him": conditional inputs.
DECLARE `reg 26(1): Suspension of payment` IS ONE OF
    `reg 26(1): The Minister must suspend the payment`
    `reg 26(1): The Minister may suspend the payment`
    `reg 26(1): The payment is not suspended under this subsection`

-- src:279 | 26 (1) The Minister shall suspend the payment of a benefit in respect of any beneficiary where it appears to him that the beneficiary is ineligible for payment of the benefit and may suspend the payment where it appears to him that further inquiry into the eligibility of the beneficiary is necessary, and such suspension shall continue until evidence satisfactory to the Minister is given that the beneficiary is eligible for the benefit.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 26(1) (src:279)
GIVEN `it appears to the Minister that the beneficiary is ineligible for payment of the benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Minister that further inquiry into the eligibility of the beneficiary is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `reg 26(1): Suspension of payment`
`reg 26(1): whether the Minister must or may suspend the payment of the benefit` `it appears to the Minister that the beneficiary is ineligible for payment of the benefit` `it appears to the Minister that further inquiry into the eligibility of the beneficiary is necessary` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it appears to the Minister that the beneficiary is ineligible for payment of the benefit` THEN `reg 26(1): The Minister must suspend the payment`
        IF `it appears to the Minister that further inquiry into the eligibility of the beneficiary is necessary` THEN `reg 26(1): The Minister may suspend the payment`
        OTHERWISE `reg 26(1): The payment is not suspended under this subsection`

@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 26(1) (src:279)
GIVEN `evidence satisfactory to the Minister has been given that the beneficiary is eligible for the benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 26(1): the suspension continues` `evidence satisfactory to the Minister has been given that the beneficiary is eligible for the benefit` MEANS
    NOT `evidence satisfactory to the Minister has been given that the beneficiary is eligible for the benefit`

-- 26(2): when a suspended payment is resumed, the Minister shall pay for any portion of the suspension period in which the
-- beneficiary was eligible. The portion is counted in days (fork F-26(2) in NOTES.md): the days of each span in which the beneficiary was eligible that lie
-- inside the suspension (the spans of eligibility are taken as not overlapping one another).
-- src:280 | (2) When payment of any benefit that has been suspended under subsection (1) is resumed, the Minister shall cause payment of the benefit to be made for any portion of the period of suspension during which the beneficiary was eligible for benefit.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 26(2) (src:280)
GIVEN `the payment of the benefit has been resumed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period of suspension` IS A `Calendar span`
      `the periods during which the beneficiary was eligible for the benefit` IS A LIST OF `Calendar span`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 26(2): the number of days of the period of suspension for which the Minister must pay the benefit` `the payment of the benefit has been resumed` `the period of suspension` `the periods during which the beneficiary was eligible for the benefit` MEANS
    IF `the payment of the benefit has been resumed`
    THEN sum (map `the days of the suspension inside` `the periods during which the beneficiary was eligible for the benefit`)
    ELSE 0
    WHERE
        `the days of the suspension inside` span MEANS
            max 0 ((Day (`oa3: the earlier of` (span's `last day`) (`the period of suspension`'s `last day`)) MINUS Day (`oa3: the later of` (span's `first day`) (`the period of suspension`'s `first day`))) PLUS 1)

§§ `Cancellation of Pension or Supplement`

-- 26.1(1): a request to cancel a pension or supplement is made to the Minister in writing no later than six months after the day
-- payment begins. The register of oas-core (item 11) names this figure as an input of ss 9.3(1) and 18.2(1) of the Act.
-- src:283 | 26.1 (1) For the purposes of subsections 9.3(1) and 18.2(1) of the Act, a request for cancellation of a pension or supplement shall be made to the Minister in writing no later than six months after the day on which payment of the pension or supplement, as the case may be, begins.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 26.1(1) (src:283)
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`reg 26.1(1): the prescribed time within which a request for cancellation may be made` MEANS
    `a limit in months` 6

@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 26.1(1) (src:283)
GIVEN `the day on which payment of the pension or supplement begins` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 26.1(1): the last day on which a request for cancellation may be made` `the day on which payment of the pension or supplement begins` MEANS
    `the day that is` `reg 26.1(1): the prescribed time within which a request for cancellation may be made` `after` `the day on which payment of the pension or supplement begins`

@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 26.1(1) (src:283)
GIVEN `the request is made to the Minister in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the request is made` IS A DATE
      `the day on which payment of the pension or supplement begins` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 26.1(1): the request for cancellation is made in time` `the request is made to the Minister in writing` `the day on which the request is made` `the day on which payment of the pension or supplement begins` MEANS
        `the request is made to the Minister in writing`
    AND `the day on which the request is made` AT MOST (`reg 26.1(1): the last day on which a request for cancellation may be made` `the day on which payment of the pension or supplement begins`)

-- 26.1(2) and (3): the amount is repaid no later than six months after the day the request is granted: (2) for a pension and any
-- related supplement or allowance, (3) for a supplement and any related allowance.
-- src:284 | (2) For the purposes of subsection 9.3(2) of the Act, the amount of any pension and related supplement or allowance shall be repaid no later than six months after the day on which the request is granted.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 26.1(2) (src:284)
GIVEN `the day on which the request is granted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 26.1(2): the last day on which the amount of the pension and related supplement or allowance must be repaid` `the day on which the request is granted` MEANS
    `the day that is` (`a limit in months` 6) `after` `the day on which the request is granted`

-- src:285 | (3) For the purposes of subsection 18.2(2) of the Act, the amount of any supplement and related allowance shall be repaid no later than six months after the day on which the request is granted.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 26.1(3) (src:285)
GIVEN `the day on which the request is granted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 26.1(3): the last day on which the amount of the supplement and related allowance must be repaid` `the day on which the request is granted` MEANS
    `the day that is` (`a limit in months` 6) `after` `the day on which the request is granted`

§§ `Recovery of Overpayments`

-- 27: for subsection 37(2.1) of the Act, an amount owing may be deducted and retained out of the whole or any portion of a benefit
-- payable to the person or their estate or succession under this Act or any other Act or program the Minister administers, in
-- any amount that does not cause undue hardship, in one payment or in instalments. What causes undue hardship is a judgment
-- the text hands to no one by name, so the largest amount that would not cause it is a plain input.
-- src:288 | 27 For the purpose of subsection 37(2.1) of the Act, an amount of indebtedness that is owing may be deducted and retained out of the whole or any portion of a benefit that is payable to the person or the person’s estate or succession, under this Act or any other Act or program administered by the Minister, that will recover the overpayment in a single payment or in instalments, in any amount that does not cause undue hardship to the person or the person’s estate or succession.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 27 (src:288)
GIVEN `the amount of indebtedness that is owing` IS A NUMBER -- out of range: section 37(2.1) (piece oa1)
      `the amount of the benefit payable to the person or the person's estate or succession under this Act or any other Act or program administered by the Minister` IS A NUMBER
      `the largest amount that does not cause undue hardship to the person or the person's estate or succession` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 27: the largest amount that may be deducted and retained out of the benefit` `the amount of indebtedness that is owing` `the amount of the benefit payable to the person or the person's estate or succession under this Act or any other Act or program administered by the Minister` `the largest amount that does not cause undue hardship to the person or the person's estate or succession` MEANS
    max 0 (min (min `the amount of indebtedness that is owing` `the amount of the benefit payable to the person or the person's estate or succession under this Act or any other Act or program administered by the Minister`) `the largest amount that does not cause undue hardship to the person or the person's estate or succession`)

§§ `Deductions from Benefits`

-- 28.1(1): for subsection 36(2) of the Act the Minister may make a deduction from a benefit if all four hold: (a) the provincial or
-- municipal authority that paid the advance, assistance or welfare payments submits a record of the payment with the person's
-- irrevocable signed consent; (b) the Minister receives them before one year after the day the consent is signed expires; (c) the
-- Minister and the authority have an agreement on the procedure; (d) the amount deducted exceeds $50.
-- src:292 | 28.1 (1) For the purposes of subsection 36(2) of the Act, the Minister may make a deduction from a benefit payable under the Act if
-- src:293 | (a) the provincial authority or the municipal authority that paid the advance, assistance or welfare payments submits a record of the payment to the Minister, together with an irrevocable consent to the deduction signed by the person receiving the payment;
-- src:294 | (b) the record and consent referred to in paragraph (a) are received by the Minister prior to the expiration of one year after the day on which the consent is signed;
-- src:295 | (c) the Minister and the provincial authority or the municipal authority that paid the advance, assistance or welfare payment referred to in paragraph (a) have concluded an agreement in respect of the procedure to be followed in submitting records and consents; and
-- src:296 | (d) the amount deducted exceeds $50.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 28.1(1) (src:292-296)
GIVEN `the authority submits a record of the payment to the Minister, together with an irrevocable consent to the deduction signed by the person receiving the payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the consent is signed` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the Minister receives the record and consent` IS A DATE
      `the Minister and the authority have concluded an agreement in respect of the procedure to be followed in submitting records and consents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount deducted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 28.1(1): the Minister may make a deduction from a benefit` `the authority submits a record of the payment to the Minister, together with an irrevocable consent to the deduction signed by the person receiving the payment` `the day on which the consent is signed` `the day on which the Minister receives the record and consent` `the Minister and the authority have concluded an agreement in respect of the procedure to be followed in submitting records and consents` `the amount deducted` MEANS
        `the authority submits a record of the payment to the Minister, together with an irrevocable consent to the deduction signed by the person receiving the payment`
    AND `the day on which the Minister receives the record and consent` AT MOST (`the day that is` (`a limit in years` 1) `after` `the day on which the consent is signed`)
    AND `the Minister and the authority have concluded an agreement in respect of the procedure to be followed in submitting records and consents`
    AND `the amount deducted` GREATER THAN 50

-- 28.1(2): if no deduction has been made, or a deduction and payment for less than might have been paid, the Minister shall not
-- authorize any other deduction and payment.
-- src:297 | (2) For the purpose of subsection 36(2) of the Act, if, for any reason, no deduction has been made or a deduction and payment have been made by the Minister for an amount that is less than the amount that might have been paid under that subsection, the Minister shall not authorize any other deduction and payment.
@ref C.R.C., c. 1246, reg 28.1(2) (src:297)
GIVEN `no deduction has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a deduction and payment have been made by the Minister for an amount that is less than the amount that might have been paid under subsection 36(2) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 28.1(2): the Minister is barred from authorizing any other deduction and payment` `no deduction has been made` `a deduction and payment have been made by the Minister for an amount that is less than the amount that might have been paid under subsection 36(2) of the Act` MEANS
        `no deduction has been made`
    OR  `a deduction and payment have been made by the Minister for an amount that is less than the amount that might have been paid under subsection 36(2) of the Act`
